{"id":"8402adceb8770037","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-prime-gap.md","title":"Prime Gap","display":"df-prime-gap — Prime Gap","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-prime-gap","aliases":["58-df-prime-gap","Prime Gap"],"display":"df-prime-gap — Prime Gap","depends_on":["[[58-df-prime-number]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-prime-gap"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-prime-gap</span><span>Prime Gap</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-prime-gap — Prime Gap"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"58-df-prime-number\">58-df-prime-number</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p:\\omega\\to\\omega\">\\(p:\\omega\\to\\omega\\)</span> (increasing enumeration of the primes)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g:\\omega\\to\\omega\">\\(g:\\omega\\to\\omega\\)</span> (consecutive-prime-gap function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Prime}\">\\(\\mathrm{Prime}\\)</span> (prime-number predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"58-df-prime-number\">58-df-prime-number</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S\\)</span> (prime-enumeration predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S\\)</span> (prime-gap sequence predicate defined in this file)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TwinPrimeGap}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{TwinPrimeGap}_S\\)</span> (twin-prime-gap predicate defined in this file)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{BoundedPrimeGaps}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{BoundedPrimeGaps}_S\\)</span> (bounded-prime-gaps predicate defined in this file)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap} \\vdash \\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S(p)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(p,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\mathrm{Prime}(p(n))\\land\\forall m,n\\in\\omega\\;(m&lt;n\\to p(m)&lt;p(n))\\land\\forall q\\in\\omega\\;(\\mathrm{Prime}(q)\\to\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(p(n)=q))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap} \\vdash \\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S(p)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(p,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\mathrm{Prime}(p(n))\\land\\forall m,n\\in\\omega\\;(m&lt;n\\to p(m)&lt;p(n))\\land\\forall q\\in\\omega\\;(\\mathrm{Prime}(q)\\to\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(p(n)=q))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}sequence} \\vdash \\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S(p)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(g,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(g(n)=p(n+1)-p(n))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}sequence} \\vdash \\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S(p)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(g,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(g(n)=p(n+1)-p(n))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}twin} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwinPrimeGap}_S(n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\\exists g,p\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\land g(n)=2)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}twin} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwinPrimeGap}_S(n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\\exists g,p\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\land g(n)=2)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}bounded} \\vdash \\operatorname{BoundedPrimeGaps}_S(g)\\leftrightarrow\\exists p\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\land\\exists b\\in\\omega\\;\\forall N\\in\\omega\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(N\\le n\\land g(n)\\le b)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}bounded} \\vdash \\operatorname{BoundedPrimeGaps}_S(g)\\leftrightarrow\\exists p\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\land\\exists b\\in\\omega\\;\\forall N\\in\\omega\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(N\\le n\\land g(n)\\le b)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Prime gap: difference between consecutive primes; its average scale near <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_n\">\\(p_n\\)</span> is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\log p_n\">\\(\\log p_n\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Twin prime: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g_n = 2\">\\(g_n = 2\\)</span> infinitely often (unproven but believed)</li>\n<li>Bounded gaps means that one finite bound occurs for infinitely many consecutive-prime gaps; this is a theorem, while the twin-prime case remains open.</li>\n<li>Elliott-Halberstam: conjecture on prime distribution; implies small gaps via Polymath</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Goldston, Graham and Pintz, Small Gaps between Primes</li>\n<li>Maynard and Tao, Bounded Gaps between Primes</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-prime-number","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-prime-number]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-prime-number","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Prime}$ (prime-number predicate, see [[58-df-prime-number]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"p:\\omega\\to\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"g:\\omega\\to\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Prime}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TwinPrimeGap}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{BoundedPrimeGaps}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap} \\vdash \\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S(p)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(p,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\mathrm{Prime}(p(n))\\land\\forall m,n\\in\\omega\\;(m<n\\to p(m)<p(n))\\land\\forall q\\in\\omega\\;(\\mathrm{Prime}(q)\\to\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(p(n)=q))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}sequence} \\vdash \\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{PrimeEnumeration}_S(p)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(g,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(g(n)=p(n+1)-p(n))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}twin} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwinPrimeGap}_S(n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\\exists g,p\\in V\\;(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\land g(n)=2)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}prime\\text{-}gap\\text{-}bounded} \\vdash \\operatorname{BoundedPrimeGaps}_S(g)\\leftrightarrow\\exists p\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{PrimeGapSeq}_S(g,p)\\land\\exists b\\in\\omega\\;\\forall N\\in\\omega\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;(N\\le n\\land g(n)\\le b)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"p_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\log p_n","display":false},{"tex":"g_n = 2","display":false}],"bytes":2364,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-981","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-prime-gap.md|58-df-prime-gap]]（batch16）"}],"outgoing":["dad686059f3ca152","36d7463d215be751"]}